('advanced-native-1885', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1885-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["相處改變了說話者對整體氣氛的感受，並非主要家具改動。"],"options":["訪客問卷已確認整體看法，說話者只在總結問卷結果。","相處改變了說話者對整體氣氛的感受，並非主要家具改動。","家具已全部換掉，說話者只在比較椅子的物料。","大家尚未開始來往，只有中心外面的宣傳改了。"]},"advanced-native-1885-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The whole place began to soften as people left notes and shared conversations over tea.","The ordinary exchanges gave the centre a warmer feeling than the furniture alone had done.","I began connecting the rooms with people and conversations rather than only a new building.","The atmosphere changed for me through the way neighbours used the space together."],"options":["The whole place began to soften as people left notes and shared conversations over tea.","The ordinary exchanges gave the centre a warmer feeling than the furniture alone had done.","I began connecting the rooms with people and conversations rather than only a new building.","The atmosphere changed for me through the way neighbours used the space together."]},"advanced-native-1885-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Her note concerns one corner; saying the whole place begins to soften would need a broader impression than she has given."],"options":["A warmer corner establishes that she has already described the atmosphere throughout the centre.","Her comment already compares several rooms and describes a broader atmosphere.","Her note concerns one corner; saying the whole place begins to soften would need a broader impression than she has given."]},"advanced-native-1885-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["所有使用者已明確表示自己感受完全相同。"],"options":["所有使用者已明確表示自己感受完全相同。","可以交代哪些日常交流促成這個印象。","整體開始給人較溫暖的感覺。"]},"advanced-native-1885-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The whole place began to soften for me through the conversations; a warmer atmosphere need not start with new furniture."],"options":["I would describe only the objects and leave out how people began using the place together.","The whole place began to soften for me through the conversations; a warmer atmosphere need not start with new furniture.","I thought the furniture list was enough to tell us whether people felt welcome in the rooms."]},"advanced-native-1885-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["To me, the whole place began to soften when visitors shared memories at the comment table and carried them into the photograph discussions. Could we keep it for the final week and ask visitors what those exchanges add?","The whole place is beginning to soften in my experience as visitors add their own recollections at that table. Before removing it, I would like us to hear what the exchanges mean to other visitors during the final week."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1886', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1886-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["共同生活帶來意義，簡單租住環境也能有家的感受。"],"options":["共同生活帶來意義，簡單租住環境也能有家的感受。","合住者已買下房屋，只有取得產權才開始做飯。","房間改成昂貴裝修，大家仍沒有共同生活。","共同用餐仍只是未實行的計劃，尚未有一起吃飯的經驗。"]},"advanced-native-1886-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["They now had something meaningful to repeat in the place where they lived.","Sharing a meal helped turn the house into a home through a memory they wanted to keep.","They began building an ordinary routine together rather than only sharing an address.","The simple rooms became connected with their own shared experience."],"options":["They now had something meaningful to repeat in the place where they lived.","Sharing a meal helped turn the house into a home through a memory they wanted to keep.","They began building an ordinary routine together rather than only sharing an address.","The simple rooms became connected with their own shared experience."]},"advanced-native-1886-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The furniture cost alone does not establish that she has turned the house into a home in the emotional sense she describes."],"options":["Paying more for furniture establishes the feeling of belonging she says is still missing.","Her stated concern is lack of space for using the furniture, rather than her missing sense of belonging.","The furniture cost alone does not establish that she has turned the house into a home in the emotional sense she describes."]},"advanced-native-1886-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["必須先買下住所並換成昂貴家具。"],"options":["生活與回憶可給地方個人意義。","必須先買下住所並換成昂貴家具。","不同人可能透過不同關係與習慣建立家的感受。"]},"advanced-native-1886-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We can turn the house into a home through how we live together, even while the building belongs to someone else."],"options":["I would assess the place only by what we can buy for it, not by the life we share there.","We can turn the house into a home through how we live together, even while the building belongs to someone else.","I thought the ownership document decided whether any shared memory in the rooms could matter."]},"advanced-native-1886-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["You helped turn the house into a home through the meals and care you shared with us, even though you did not own the building. Leaving can still hurt, but it does not make those years less real.","The evenings in your kitchen helped turn the house into a home for us, not just an address on a contract. Thank you for that welcome; I hope you can carry its meaning with you while making room for the sadness too."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
