('advanced-native-1892', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1892-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["實習提供初步進入與學習，但未承諾長期職位。"],"options":["館方已給永久職位邀請，實習只是正式到職前一段。","實習申請仍未回覆，說話者還未進過檔案館。","館方只答應寄公開資料，沒有安排說話者進館實習。","實習提供初步進入與學習，但未承諾長期職位。"]},"advanced-native-1892-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It was a first opportunity to experience the field from inside the organisation.","I gained an introduction that I would still need to build on.","It gave me a foot in the door at the archive, without guaranteeing a permanent job.","I could learn the daily routine and get to know the people doing the work."],"options":["It was a first opportunity to experience the field from inside the organisation.","I gained an introduction that I would still need to build on.","It gave me a foot in the door at the archive, without guaranteeing a permanent job.","I could learn the daily routine and get to know the people doing the work."]},"advanced-native-1892-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The application alone does not establish a foot in the door yet; we need to know whether an actual opportunity has been offered."],"options":["The application alone does not establish a foot in the door yet; we need to know whether an actual opportunity has been offered.","Sending the form establishes that she has already begun learning inside the organisation.","She has received an invitation to join the archive, but is asking for more time before accepting."]},"advanced-native-1892-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["長期職位與之後升遷都已獲保證。"],"options":["長期職位與之後升遷都已獲保證。","之後仍可能要學習、申請或建立經驗。","有初步進入或接觸機會。"]},"advanced-native-1892-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["A foot in the door can be useful without being a permanent offer; I can learn the routine and decide what experience to build next."],"options":["A foot in the door can be useful without being a permanent offer; I can learn the routine and decide what experience to build next.","I thought the only valuable introduction was one that already guaranteed a lasting role.","I thought I had been offered a lasting role, rather than only this short introduction."]},"advanced-native-1892-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Thank you for giving me a foot in the door through the design discussion; I now have a clearer idea of what I need to learn. Would it be appropriate to send one question about the model-making process after I review my notes?","That introduction was a foot in the door, not a team position, and I value the chance to see the work being discussed. Could I ask a brief follow-up about the materials when I have read the notes carefully?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1893', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1893-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["這是兩人按需要變化的經歷，不是人人必須照走的次序。"],"options":["這是兩人按需要變化的經歷，不是人人必須照走的次序。","敘述已規定每個家庭必須在相同年齡買樓。","兩人一直住在原房間，沒有提過其他安排。","他們原已按固定購買日期作決定，並沒有考慮工作地點。"]},"advanced-native-1893-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["They presented a personal sequence without claiming it was the required sequence for other households.","The housing journey followed changing needs, rather than a fixed route for everyone.","They moved from sharing a rented room to a longer stay near work.","Their account connected the choices with what mattered at each stage."],"options":["They presented a personal sequence without claiming it was the required sequence for other households.","The housing journey followed changing needs, rather than a fixed route for everyone.","They moved from sharing a rented room to a longer stay near work.","Their account connected the choices with what mattered at each stage."]},"advanced-native-1893-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The housing journey can change direction with circumstances; the shorter arrangement alone does not establish personal failure."],"options":["The account says a permanent purchase has already replaced the short stay, rather than describing the short stay as the present arrangement.","The housing journey can change direction with circumstances; the shorter arrangement alone does not establish personal failure.","The shorter stay should be ranked below the earlier arrangement even though it fits the person’s current work needs."]},"advanced-native-1893-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["所有人都必須按同一次序由租住走向購買。"],"options":["可敘述一個人或家庭隨時間的住屋變化。","所有人都必須按同一次序由租住走向購買。","需要與情況改變時，路線也可能不同。"]},"advanced-native-1893-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The housing journey does not have to follow one route; I would compare the needs and commitments at each stage rather than match your sequence."],"options":["I would rank the choices only by whether they move towards ownership, without considering why they were made.","The housing journey does not have to follow one route; I would compare the needs and commitments at each stage rather than match your sequence.","I assumed your sequence would suit me before comparing the needs behind our different choices."]},"advanced-native-1893-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Could the housing journey be shown on an open timeline rather than three preprinted stages? Interviewees could add the dates and changes that matter to them without having to fit a route we have chosen in advance.","I would leave space for people to describe the housing journey in their own order, using dated events rather than fixed labels about ownership. That would let the display include changes of direction as well as longer stays."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1894', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1894-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["早期經驗影響後來的待人方式，但這裏沒有說是唯一成因。"],"options":["她主要記得讀書會有名氣，沒有指出後來的具體做法。","早期經驗影響後來的待人方式，但這裏沒有說是唯一成因。","她在成年後才第一次遇見這個讀書會，沒有早年參與。","她後來已完全反對讓學員提問，跟早期經驗相反。"]},"advanced-native-1894-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["An experience from her formative years had helped shape how she welcomed younger learners’ questions.","She could see a link between the early reading group and her later response to uncertainty.","Being allowed to ask questions had become part of what she valued when listening to others.","The early group mattered to her later habits, without explaining every influence on them."],"options":["An experience from her formative years had helped shape how she welcomed younger learners’ questions.","She could see a link between the early reading group and her later response to uncertainty.","Being allowed to ask questions had become part of what she valued when listening to others.","The early group mattered to her later habits, without explaining every influence on them."]},"advanced-native-1894-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Learning at forty can be important, but this account does not establish an experience from her formative years."],"options":["Calling the lesson important establishes that it occurred during childhood or adolescence.","The new editing method is described as something she had already practised as a child.","Learning at forty can be important, but this account does not establish an experience from her formative years."]},"advanced-native-1894-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["之後人生不再可能學習或改變。"],"options":["之後人生不再可能學習或改變。","仍需具體資料說明經驗怎樣有影響。","早年經驗可能參與習慣與態度形成。"]},"advanced-native-1894-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["My formative years helped shape my habits, but I can still examine them and learn different ways of listening now."],"options":["I thought adapting those habits would contradict the early influence, so I had not considered trying a different approach.","My formative years helped shape my habits, but I can still examine them and learn different ways of listening now.","I thought an early influence meant my present habits no longer needed reflection."]},"advanced-native-1894-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Could we label this section ‘formative years’ rather than suggest that her future was already settled? The childhood photographs can sit beside later accounts of changing work and ideas, so visitors see influence as well as development.","Her formative years deserve attention, but I would not arrange the display as if every later choice followed automatically. Could we leave room for the adult changes she describes in the interview?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1895', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1895-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["學生建議實際影響清單，但不是獨自控制全部決定。"],"options":["學生已獲獨自決定所有場地及人手的權力。","職員在聽意見前已拒絕任何清單改動。","學生建議實際影響清單，但不是獨自控制全部決定。","學生只被告知主題，沒有提出任何建議。"]},"advanced-native-1895-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Its ideas helped shape which themes were considered.","The panel influenced the choice while staff continued to share the final decisions.","It contributed more than a ceremonial comment, but did not decide every practical matter alone.","It had a strong say in the themes because its proposals changed the shortlist."],"options":["Its ideas helped shape which themes were considered.","The panel influenced the choice while staff continued to share the final decisions.","It contributed more than a ceremonial comment, but did not decide every practical matter alone.","It had a strong say in the themes because its proposals changed the shortlist."]},"advanced-native-1895-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Speaking time alone does not establish that they have a strong say in the decision; we need to know how their input can affect the choice."],"options":["Speaking time alone does not establish that they have a strong say in the decision; we need to know how their input can affect the choice.","The length of their comments establishes that the committee must adopt their preferred option.","The record already identifies an adopted proposal that changed the shortlist."]},"advanced-native-1895-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["必定可獨自否決所有其他人的想法。"],"options":["必定可獨自否決所有其他人的想法。","可有多方共同參與最後決定。","對選擇有相當影響。"]},"advanced-native-1895-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["I had a strong say in the shortlist through the proposals we adopted, even though the final decision was shared."],"options":["I thought influence counted only when nobody else took part in the final choice.","I thought the staff fixed the shortlist first and only invited us to hear the result afterwards.","I had a strong say in 